<onlyinclude>A '''signal''' is a varying quantity or sequence used to represent, convey or observe something. A microphone voltage represents changes in air pressure; a sequence of bits may represent a message. A signal need not be intentionally sent: an instrument can observe a natural process.

== Explanation ==
Signals may be continuous in time, sampled at discrete times, or encoded into discrete values. Sampling and quantization are distinct operations. Noise, distortion and the characteristics of the measurement device affect what a receiver can recover. A measured pattern is not automatically meaningful or causal.

